Hi,

These patches make some changes to mixer on Audigy 1 and Audigy 2.

Changes:
- new FX bus allocated for Wave Stereo playback ("Wave Playback=20
Volume")
- new "Master Playback Volume" control - controls output volume for=20
all channels (implemented using DSP code)
- new controls "PCM Front Playback Volume", "PCM Surround Playback=20
Volume", "PCM Center Playback Volume", "PCM LFE Playback Volume" for=20
multi-channel (5.1) playback
- new controls "Front Playback Volume", "Surround Playback=20
Volume", "Center Playback Volume", "LFE Playback Volume" - there are=20
just before master volume - controls mix from PCM (5.1) and Stereo=20
Mix (Stereo Wave, AC97, ...)
- new controls "Stereo Mix Front Playback Volume", "Stereo Mix=20
Surround Playback Volume", "Stereo Mix Center Playback=20
Volume", "Stereo Mix LFE Playback Volume" - used do control volume of=20
mix from stereo sources (make mirroring to 5.1 for stereo)
Audigy 1:
- removed AC97 control "Master Volume Playback", "Master Mono Volume=20
Playback", "PCM Volume Playback", "PCM Out Path & Mute" - there are=20
unused
- uses Philips 6 channel DAC for all channels, WARNING: all analog=20
sources are routed throught DSP (if you want listen line in you must=20
set "AC97 Playback Volume" and "(" set capture on "(" "Line in"=20
and "Capture" ")" or "(" capture on "Mix" and volume for "Line in" ")"
  using Philis DAC has some advantage - Same volume levels for all=20
channels, I think better signal, ..)
    - analog signals can by routed to all channles
  disadvantage - all analog signals must be routed throught DSP -=20
(confusing selecting analog inputs and volumes for analogs inputs)

I tested 5.1 playback, wave stereo playback midi playback and analog=20
playback.
I hope I don't break something (OSS mixer, AC3 playback, optical=20
input, output, coaxial input, output) - not tested.
Names are not very well choosen (some needs rename).
Maybe I can remove "Front Playback Volume", "Surround Playback=20
Volume", "Center Playback Volume", "LFE Playback Volume" and use only=20
controls for "PCM" and "Stereo Mix"

devices:
front - routed throught front channels of 5.1 PCM ("PCM Front"=20
controls volume)
rear - routed throught rear channels of 5.1 PCM ("PCM Surround"=20
controls volume)
center_lfe - routed throught center, lfe channels of 5.1 PCM ("PCM=20
Center" and "PCM LFE" controls volume)
default (stereo) - routed to stereo mix ("Wave" controls volume)
Any suggestions, bugs, ...

